ro1348</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Head IM, Jones DM, Roling WFM (2006) Marine micro-organisms make a meal of oil. Nature Rev Microbiol 4:173&#x02013;182 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16489346</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Heiss-Blanquet</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Benoit</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Mar&#x000e9;chaux</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Monot</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Assessing the role of alkane hydroxylase genotypes in environmental samples by competitive PCR</article-title><source>J Appl Microbiol</source><year>2005</year><volume>99</volume><fpage>1392</fpage><lpage>1403</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/j.1365-2672.2005.02715.x</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Heiss-Blanquet S, Benoit Y, Mar&#x000e9;chaux C, Monot F (2005) Assessing the role of alkane hydroxylase genotypes in environmental samples by competitive PCR. J Appl Microbiol 99:1392&#x02013;1403 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16313412</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Henstra</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name><name><surname>Stams</surname><given-names>AJM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Novel physiological features of <italic>Carboxydothermus hydrogenoformans</italic> and <italic>Thermoterrabacterium ferrireducens</italic></article-title><source>Appl Env Microbiol</source><year>2004</year><volume>70</volume><fpage>7236</fpage><lpage>7240</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1128/AEM.70.12.7236-7240.2004</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Henstra AM, Stams AJM (2004) Novel physiological features of Carboxydothermus hydrogenoformans and Th